questions.explanation:
Displacement is the algebraic sum of the areas under the velocity-time graph.

$$
\text{Area}_{0-2s} = 8 \times 2 = 16 \text{ m}
$$

$$
\text{Area}_{2-4s} = (-4) \times 2 = -8 \text{ m}
$$

$$
\text{Area}_{4-8s} = 4 \times 4 = 16 \text{ m}
$$

$$
\text{Area}_{8-10s} = (-4) \times 2 = -8 \text{ m}
$$

$$
\text{Total Displacement} = 16 + (-8) + 16 + (-8) = 16 \text{ m}
$$

Distance is the sum of the magnitudes of the areas under the velocity-time graph.

$$
\text{Distance} = |16| + |-8| + |16| + |-8| = 16 + 8 + 16 + 8 = 48 \text{ m}
$$

$$
\text{Ratio} = \frac{\text{Displacement}}{\text{Distance}} = \frac{16}{48} = \frac{1}{3}
$$

